        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "Younger Okinawan speakers are L1 Japanese speakers, and L2 South-Central Okinawan learners (most people under 40 who learn are involved in traditional Okinawan culture, like the theater, with a growing number of language activists). And basically no children learn it at home from their parents, though there have been efforts to establish a language nest. [Endangerment.Certainty: 0.8]",
